  "result": "**Quick summary:** a language model can only write text. It can't click, search or book anything itself. Tool calling is how it asks something else to do those things for it.\n\n**Analogy: a referee and VAR**\n- The referee (the model) is on the pitch and can't see the replay.\n- VAR (the tool) can check footage, but only when asked.\n- The referee decides whether to ask, and what to ask: \"check for offside on that goal.\"\n- The request is just a message. The referee doesn't run the replay.\n- VAR does the checking and sends back a result: \"offside, 2 cm.\"\n- The referee reads it, then makes the call or asks for another check. That repeat is the agent loop you already know.\n\n**Mapped to your makerspace assistant**\n- Student: \"Is the laser cutter free Friday?\"\n- Model's message: \"Call the calendar tool for the laser cutter, Friday.\"\n- Your code runs the lookup and sends the answer back as text.\n- Model replies to the student using that answer.\n\n**Where the analogy stops:** a referee knows what VAR can do from experience. The model only knows what each tool's written description tells it.\n\n**Quick check:** in this setup, who actually runs the calendar lookup: the model or your code?",
